# Google Workspace safety

## Read-only / draft default

When Workspace craft is authorized, these are fine without a mutate/outbound
verb:

- Gmail: `search_gmail_messages`, `get_gmail_message_content`,
  `get_gmail_messages_content_batch`, `get_gmail_thread_content`,
  `get_gmail_threads_content_batch`, `get_gmail_attachment_content`,
  `list_gmail_labels`, `list_gmail_filters`, `draft_gmail_message`
- Drive: `search_drive_files`, `list_drive_items`, `get_drive_file_content`,
  `get_drive_file_download_url`, `get_drive_file_permissions`,
  `get_drive_shareable_link`, `check_drive_file_public_access`
- Calendar: `list_calendars`, `get_events`, `query_freebusy`
- Docs: `search_docs`, `list_docs_in_folder`, `get_doc_content`,
  `get_doc_as_markdown`, `inspect_doc_structure`, `debug_table_structure`,
  `list_document_comments`
- Sheets: `list_spreadsheets`, `get_spreadsheet_info`, `read_sheet_values`,
  `list_sheet_tables`, `list_spreadsheet_comments`

Do **not** do any of the following unless the user gave an explicit verb this
turn naming the target (message/thread, file, event, doc/sheet, label, filter):

| Mutate / outbound | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Send mail | `send_gmail_message` |
| Apply / remove labels on mail | `modify_gmail_message_labels`,
  `batch_modify_gmail_message_labels` |
| Create / update / delete labels | `manage_gmail_label` |
| Create / delete filters | `manage_gmail_filter` |
| Share / revoke / transfer ownership | `manage_drive_access`
  (`grant`, `grant_batch`, `update`, `revoke`, `transfer_owner`, `list`) |
| Anyone-with-link / link role | `set_drive_file_permissions` (`link_sharing`
  `reader`/`commenter`/`writer`) |
| Trash Drive file | `update_drive_file` with `trashed=true` |
| Create / update / delete calendar event | `manage_event`
  (`create`/`update`/`delete`); RSVP is also mutate |
| Create calendar | `create_calendar` |
| OOO / focus create/update/delete | `manage_out_of_office`,
  `manage_focus_time` (non-list actions) |
| Create / rewrite Docs or Sheets | `create_doc`, `create_spreadsheet`,
  `create_sheet`, `modify_doc_text`, `batch_update_doc`,
  `find_and_replace_doc`, `modify_sheet_values` (write or `clear_values`),
  `append_table_rows`, `resize_sheet_dimensions` delete/hide rows-cols |
| Export Doc to PDF | `export_doc_to_pdf` |
| Auth bootstrap | `start_google_auth` only when MCP reports auth is required |

`list` on `manage_drive_access` is read-only once a `file_id` is known.

## Irreversible — confirm blast radius

Before proceeding when clearly authorized:

| Action | State risk |
| --- | --- |
| `send_gmail_message` | Mail leaves the mailbox; cannot unsend via MCP |
| `share_type=anyone` / link_sharing on | File becomes reachable without a named
  account |
| `transfer_owner` | You may lose control of the file |
| `trashed=true` / event `delete` | Removes from active view; recovery is
  manual |
| `modify_sheet_values` + `clear_values` | Wipes the named A1 range |
| `resize_sheet_dimensions` `delete_rows` /
  `delete_row_range` / `delete_columns` | Drops sheet structure and data |
| Filter / label `delete` | Changes inbox routing for future mail |

State the object (subject / file name / event summary / range) and consequence
in one sentence, then act only if authorization already covers that loss.

## Account and secrets posture

1. Pass `user_google_email` as the connected MCP documents (example pattern:
   `admin@nodadyoushutup.com`). Never invent a different address.
2. Never ask the operator to paste OAuth tokens, app passwords, or refresh
   tokens into chat. Prefer `start_google_auth` when the namespace requires it.
3. Redact secrets, tokens, and full mailbox dumps from chat excerpts.
4. Do not broaden sharing beyond the role and audience the user named.
5. Bare product name alone is not a send / share / delete authorization.
